{
  "info": {
    "name": "Instagram Automation API (v2.0 - Complete)",
    "_postman_id": "4c7cdcc2-2e10-4cc3-8b48-57965acc5840",
    "description": "Comprehensive Postman collection for the Instagram Automation API.\n\n### Features\n- **Authentication**: JWT Login & Token Validation with automated session saving\n- **Dashboard**: Real-time stats & overview of trends, posts, and analytics\n- **Trends Management**: Scrape and rank trends from Google Trends and Google News RSS\n- **Post Generation & Publishing**: End-to-end AI workflow (Groq text generation + ClusterProtocol/Pollinations image composition + Meta Graph API Instagram Publishing)\n- **Instagram Token Management**: Token health inspector, token bootstrapping & token refresh\n- **Analytics Insights**: Sync and view post engagement metrics (impressions, reach, likes, comments)\n- **Dynamic Settings & Niches**: Configure API keys, niches, cron schedules, and timezones\n\n### Instructions\n1. Set your environment to **Instagram Automation - Local**.\n2. Run **Auth -> 1. Admin Login** first. The collection automatically saves the returned JWT `authToken` to your environment.\n3. All subsequent requests automatically inherit the `authToken`.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "bearer",
    "bearer": [
      {
        "key": "token",
        "value": "{{authToken}}",
        "type": "string"
      }
    ]
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "baseUrl",
      "value": "http://localhost:3000/api",
      "type": "string"
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "1. Authentication",
      "description": "JWT-based authentication for administrative dashboard and operations.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "1. Admin Login",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"Status code is 200/201\", function () {",
                  "    pm.expect(pm.response.code).to.be.oneOf([200, 201]);",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "var jsonData = pm.response.json();",
                  "if (jsonData && jsonData.data && jsonData.data.accessToken) {",
                  "    pm.environment.set(\"authToken\", jsonData.data.accessToken);",
                  "    console.log(\"Saved authToken to environment successfully\");",
                  "} else if (jsonData && jsonData.accessToken) {",
                  "    pm.environment.set(\"authToken\", jsonData.accessToken);",
                  "    console.log(\"Saved authToken to environment successfully\");",
                  "}"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            },
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{adminEmail}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{adminPassword}}\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/login",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["auth", "login"]
            },
            "description": "Logs in with the admin credentials configured in `.env` (default: admin@automation.local / Admin@12345). Auto-saves the returned JWT token to `authToken`."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "2. Get Current User Profile (Validate Session)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"Status code is 200\", function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "});"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/me",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["auth", "me"]
            },
            "description": "Verifies the current JWT token session and returns user email and role."
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ]
    },
